    {
      "id": "survey-akari-acua",
      "subject": "AKARI thermal diameter as an alternative scale",
      "status": "excluded",
      "finding": "[AKARI AcuA](https://data.darts.isas.jaxa.jp/pub/akari/AKARI-IRC_Catalogue_AllSky_AcuA_1.0/) — retained for comparison; the selected archive model has a physical size calibration. Its fitted nonrotating-sphere diameter is 87.84 ± 0.97 km. Formal catalog error omits additional shape, spin and thermal-model effects; no total confidence interval is invented. The original catalogue row for asteroid 97 was retrieved again and matched field-for-field with the retained row, including diameter, reported error and detection count.",
      "revisitWhen": "A source-specific comparison with the selected shape and physical calibration justifies changing the adopted scale.",
      "evidence": [
        "https://github.com/layoutit/css.earth/blob/d1374f2b47d1e24d7cc08368644c1a5c9444f8f0/src/objects/klotho/README.md",
